WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.900
Treasure Island

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.360
<i>The man who arrived at the inn,</i>

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.910
<i>Billy Bones, was indeed a pirate.</i>

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.040
<i>On top of that, his former companions were after him for some reason.</i>

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.090
<i>At first, Black Dog came.</i>

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:29.720
<i>And a little later, a strange blind man appeared.</i>

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.650
Young man,
excuse me for asking this,

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:44.090
but can you give me your hand and guide me to the creek?

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:45.260
Of course!

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:49.570
What are you doing?!

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:54.000
Laddie, bring me to Billy.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:07.730
Sir, dinner is served.

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.210
I'll wait in the dining room.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:32.690
Let go of me!
You'll break my arm!

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:34.410
I can't see anything.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:39.090
But you can see just fine,
even with a broken arm.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:40.710
S-So what!?

00:01:55.560 --> 00:02:00.350
In other words, obey me nicely and I won't have to be mean.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.600
I-I understand...

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:09.720
Madam, isn't there going to be rum with dinner?

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.100
You really believe that it'll kill me?

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.950
Fine, I understand!

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:36.030
Treasure
Island

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:35.830
Takarajima

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:44.640
saa ikou

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:44.640
Come, let's go

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.730
yume ni mita shima heto

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.730
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.570
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.570
Across the waves, on the wind

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:54.450
umi hedeyou

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:54.450
We'll travel the oceans

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:57.370
ikute ni wa

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:57.370
Many of us

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:00.370
minna mada shiranai

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:00.370
Still don't know of

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:04.120
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:04.120
The days and nights full of mystery

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.620
matte iru darou

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.620
That await us there

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:10.130
itsumo shinji you

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:10.130
We must always have trust

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.380
magokoro wo

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.380
And be sincere

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:19.640
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:19.640
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:22.770
tade hitotsu no

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:22.770
I only...

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.190
akogare dake wa

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.190
...have one desire

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:28.480
doko no dare ni mo

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:28.480
And no one...

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:35.190
kese wa shinai sa

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:35.190
...will ever take it away

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:41.740
tade hitotsu no

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:41.740
I only...

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:45.040
akogare dake wa

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:45.040
...have one desire

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.370
doko no dare ni mo

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.370
And no one...

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:54.300
kese wa shinai sa

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:54.300
...will ever take it away

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:05.200
episode

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:05.200
The thrown down crutches

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:20.560
Jim's really late.
Where could he be?

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:24.320
Sir?

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:28.280
I'll go get the medicine from Dr. Livesey.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:31.000
That medicine...
Is it for me?

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.060
Yes.
Jim will return soon,

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:36.880
so if you need something, just ask him.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:38.360
Sure.
Ma'am!

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.480
When you see that quack, ask him this:

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:44.930
When is it safe for me
to drink alcohol again?

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:46.530
I will.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:57.850
There's the rum!

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:05.450
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest...

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:10.560
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of rum!

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.370
Drink and the devil...

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.790
...had done for the r—

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:17.290
That's the same song
Captain Billy sang.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.420
Everyone knows it.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:23.710
Any man who's been drinking with pirates, that is.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:31.930
Drink and the devil had done for the rest...

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:47.120
Is that you Billy?

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:51.450
Yes, it is you.
I recognize the way you breathe.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.520
What's wrong, Billy Bones?

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:59.920
Your old friend Blind Pew
has come to visit...

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.450
...and you can't even say hello, eh?

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:15.160
What are you waiting for, Billy?

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:17.440
Come on, let's drink to our reunion.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:20.900
Th-The doctor has prohibited me to drink.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.580
<i>You</i>  have stopped drinking?

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.160
Come and see me anyway.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:32.890
You don't suspect a poor, blind man like me, eh?

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.270
I won't keep you very long.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.560
Billy, this is for you.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.030
Please hold out your left hand.

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:01.730
Come, come, no need for that!
Put away your sword.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:04.480
Today, I am here as a messenger.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:09.200
Come, Billy Bones, hold out your left hand.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:51.030
I-It's over. They have
given me the black spot.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.360
The Black Spot?

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:56.530
It means that I am banished from pirating...

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:59.920
...and that I don't have very long left.

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:03.250
All the pirates of the world are after me now.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:08.240
They are entitled to kill anyone
who has received the Black Spot.

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:12.470
Be it during dinner,
while sleeping or from behind...

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:17.100
I need alcohol!
Bring me rum, Jim!

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.370
I need alcohol!

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.270
Bring me rum, Jim.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:25.480
Jim!

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:34.070
P-Please, rum!

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:35.160
No!

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:38.010
Dr. Livesey forbids you!

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:39.580
Rum! Rum!

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:40.780
A-Alcohol!

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:45.290
...alcohol!

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:50.760
Captain Billy, stop!

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:10.820
Givin' me the Black Spot, dammit...

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:12.990
Like hell I let myself get killed!

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:19.450
I-I am Billy Bones, first mate of
Great Pirate Captain Flint...

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:23.100
Who they hell do those cheap buccaneers think they are?!

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:27.730
You bunch of wretches!
I'm more than ready for you!

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:42.440
There's something written on the back.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:48.480
"You have until 10 O'clock tonight."

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:57.070
What, 10 O'clock?

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:09.460
I-I have three hours left...

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:22.930
I'm waiting for you, one-legged man!

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:39.360
Captain!
Captain Billy!

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:56.420
Look, Pew.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:59.590
Oh, that's right.
You can't see anything.

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:03.490
The boss has come to greet us in person.

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:35.880
It's alright, his heart is still beating.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:38.150
Benbow, I'm counting on you.

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:40.080
I'm going to find Dr. Livesey.

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:48.020
Hoist the sails, men!

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:52.350
Prepare to set sail!
To the island of treasures!

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:53.600
Island of treasures?

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:56.190
Oh, is that you, old sailor?

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:58.440
It's old Captain Flint!

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:05.780
I've finally found you after all this time.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:07.550
Boy, did I miss you.

00:12:07.550 --> 00:12:12.920
Don't you worry. What you entrusted me with is safe in my chest.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:19.960
Captain!
Hang on, Captain Billy!

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:22.130
Captain!

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:26.100
Release the sails.
A storm's coming, men.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:34.910
Don't be afraid,
we all will die one day!

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:36.730
Helm to starboard!

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:04.340
Jim...

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:05.260
Captain!

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:09.560
Hold on!
I'll go find Dr. Livesey!

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:15.940
He can draw your blood and you'll get better!

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:18.520
Jim!

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:19.860
Wait...

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:22.480
I want you to take this.

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:24.820
The key to your chest?!

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:30.770
It is. Inside you'll find a valuable document wrapped in oil paper.

00:13:30.770 --> 00:13:33.900
I beg you...
Don't let them take it.

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:35.730
If you do what I say,

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:38.820
I will let you have a large portion of the treasure.

00:13:38.820 --> 00:13:40.750
Treasure?
Did you say treasure?

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:45.510
Captain!

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:49.970
The island!
I can see it!

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:57.670
Look, my mateys, over there!

00:13:57.670 --> 00:14:00.580
Behind those waves.
Do you see it, mateys?

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:04.150
It's so beautiful...

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:07.640
See, that usual terrible storm has stopped.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:10.950
<i>Jim!</i>

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:15.220
<i>Grant Billy Bones' final wish!
Get me a single glass of rum...</i>

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:41.940
I'm back.

00:14:44.430 --> 00:14:46.320
Jim!
What happened?!

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:50.140
It's the captain!
He's dead!

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:07.010
Boss, we are ready to depart.

00:15:07.350 --> 00:15:09.010
We await your orders.

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:17.670
Hurry, mother, they're coming!

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:19.640
They're coming to attack at 10 O'clock!

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:21.430
Who are they?

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:24.980
Those guys!
Black Dog and Blind Pew!

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:26.480
And leading them, the one-legged man!

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:27.930
Them pirates!

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:31.750
I'll go back to the village.
We need help!

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:37.040
Wait, you idiot!

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:41.670
Mother! Come with me!
If you stay here, you'll be in danger!

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:44.920
They may attack before I come back!

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:47.160
Don't worry about me, Jim.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:51.390
I will protect our home until help arrives.

00:15:51.390 --> 00:15:54.860
No, no!
This time, it's serious!

00:15:54.860 --> 00:15:56.420
After all, our enemies are all like—

00:15:58.900 --> 00:15:59.710
Like that.

00:15:59.710 --> 00:16:00.560
Get it?

00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:05.030
Anyway, both of us must go!
Together!

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:06.940
You idiot!

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:08.730
I forgot to put out the fire!

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:23.720
I'm coming!

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:40.680
It's the pirates! They're attacking the Admiral Benbow Inn!

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:41.880
Please help us!

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:45.300
They used to be with the pirate Flint!

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:47.480
What, men of the pirate Flint?

00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:51.200
Did you say Captain Flint?
That terror?

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:53.410
Ouch, my stomach, I'm sick!

00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:00.470
We can't measure up to Flint's men.

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:02.700
I can't be involved in this!

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.080
We're sorry.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.250
I mean, like, what could we possibly do?

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:12.350
Mother, you better go sleep at our friend's.

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:14.220
And what are you going to do?

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:18.030
It's obvious.
I'm going back to the inn.

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:20.440
I am a man, so I have to fight!

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:23.890
Let's go, Benbow!
Come with me, if you're a man!

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:26.490
Jim, wait!

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:27.350
Lilly!

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:32.350
Here, take it.
Take this with you!

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:33.770
It's loaded.

00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:35.950
It's my grandfather's.

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:37.190
It's magnificent!

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:39.640
Grandfather surely could have helped,

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:42.930
but he hasn't come back.
I apologize.

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:46.340
That's okay. With this
I can stand up to them!

00:17:47.740 --> 00:17:49.250
Thank you, Lilly!

00:17:55.580 --> 00:17:56.430
Mother!

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:58.470
What do you think you're doing?

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:01.400
For cryin' out loud, this is nothing I can't handle.

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:14.180
It's okay, mother.
No one is here yet.

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:20.250
I hear footsteps...

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:35.710
Don't move, or I'll shoot!

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:40.140
M-Mercy! H-Have mercy!

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:41.850
I'll give you what you want, but please spare me!

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:45.400
I beg you... Please have mercy.
Don't kill me!

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:48.010
Sir, you're not a pirate?

00:18:48.010 --> 00:18:50.270
Me, a pirate?

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:53.780
Why would you say that?
I am just a simple traveler.

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:57.190
I'm just looking for somewhere to spend the night.

00:18:57.190 --> 00:18:59.630
R-Really?
Is that true?

00:18:59.630 --> 00:19:01.310
Who are you, kid?

00:19:01.310 --> 00:19:04.240
I-I am... well, the son of the innkeeper.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:06.820
What, this is your inn?!

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:09.620
You wanted to steal me money, didn't ya?!

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:12.340
Excuse me, please let me explain...

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:15.350
I don't want to hear it!
Shut up!

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:16.340
I am outraged!

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:18.470
What's this?

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:26.480
I'm outta here!

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:32.880
The poor guy, we can't leave him like this.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:36.410
Yes, let's put him on
his bed upstairs, mother.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:43.830
This is bad! We have only half an hour before they're here!

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:47.790
Jim!

00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:52.710
The captain asked me to keep the contents of his chest safe!

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:13.560
My, it's a captain's uniform!

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:16.990
What's more, it's brand new.
There's also a matching hat.

00:20:16.990 --> 00:20:21.280
<i>I see, the captain had dreamed of returning to the sea.</i>

00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:23.240
A quadrant,

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:24.750
a compass...

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:26.240
...and a telescope.

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:28.540
Mother, you okay?

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:31.000
A knife,

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:33.230
coconut...

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:34.350
...and seashells.

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:39.760
Color me surprised...
Sailors really are all alike.

00:20:39.760 --> 00:20:42.800
Your father also kept precious things like these.

00:20:44.350 --> 00:20:46.600
And a pair of striped underpants! Brand new!

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:52.850
<i>Jim!</i>

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:56.350
<i>There you'll find a valuable document wrapped in oil paper.</i>

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:59.070
<i>I beg you, don't let them take it.</i>

00:21:01.060 --> 00:21:01.690
That's it!

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:03.990
No mistake, this is it!

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:17.100
It's gold! Jim, you think we can use it to pay his bill?

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:20.340
Why not? He said he would pay upon departure.

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:31.840
Let's see...
These are Spanish doubloons,

00:21:31.840 --> 00:21:34.480
so if you convert to pounds,
that makes...

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:36.770
We'll just keep everything, Mom!

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:38.510
No, we shouldn't, Jim!

00:21:38.510 --> 00:21:41.710
At the Admiral Benbow Inn,
we don't rob our customers.

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:45.700
Let's see,
the captain stayed 29 nights...

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:56.590
Mother, did you hear anything just now?!

00:21:57.270 --> 00:21:58.080
No.

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:32.500
To      be        continued

00:22:33.490 --> 00:22:38.530
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:33.490 --> 00:22:38.530
Hey sea breeze

00:22:38.530 --> 00:22:44.340
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:38.530 --> 00:22:44.340
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:45.560 --> 00:22:50.550
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:45.560 --> 00:22:50.550
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:50.550 --> 00:22:55.990
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:50.550 --> 00:22:55.990
A word to my dear mother

00:22:55.990 --> 00:23:01.400
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:55.990 --> 00:23:01.400
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:06.860
kaban ippai no

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:06.860
And that my bag filled

00:23:06.860 --> 00:23:12.490
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:06.860 --> 00:23:12.490
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:18.350
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:18.350
Will be brought back

00:23:19.440 --> 00:23:24.940
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:19.440 --> 00:23:24.940
The sunset on my back

00:23:24.940 --> 00:23:30.830
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:24.940 --> 00:23:30.830
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:30.830 --> 00:23:40.550
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:30.830 --> 00:23:40.550
I blow out a whistle

00:23:45.250 --> 00:23:47.550
The assault of the pirates has started!

00:23:47.550 --> 00:23:50.270
They break windows, overturn tables.

00:23:50.270 --> 00:23:53.040
All in all, they completely destroy
the Admiral Benbow inn.

00:23:53.680 --> 00:23:58.390
When they realize, while searching Billy's chest,
that what they're looking for is gone,

00:23:58.390 --> 00:24:00.390
they become even more enraged.

00:24:01.790 --> 00:24:04.790
In fact, I am the one who has it.

00:24:05.270 --> 00:24:06.800
Next time on Treasure Island:

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:08.630
"I've got the Map to Treasure Island!"

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:09.910
Awesome!

